# systemd presets for the Open AD Kit X5H image (issue #120 M7).
# Installed by aib/x5h-rootfs.aib.yml to /etc/systemd/system-preset/.
#
# This file enables six units: SSH daemon, role banner, container store
# mount, NPU work partition mount, NPU service, and CR52 remoteproc.
#
# THE QUADLET UNITS ARE NOT LISTED, and adding them would be a no-op that
# reads like a decision. Quadlet generates their .service units at boot and
# writes the default.target.wants symlink itself for every .container that
# carries an [Install] section -- that is what "enabled" means for a
# generated unit, and no preset line adds to or subtracts from it. The only
# lever over that set is the unit files, not this file.
#
# None of the five awf-oak-*.container units carries an [Install] section
# any more, so none of them comes up on its own. See selfboot.md, "Which
# stack owns a boot", for why the role draws that line.
#
# rpmsg-eth.service IS installed by the manifest and is deliberately NOT
# enabled here -- a standing human ruling. Its daemon binary
# (/usr/local/bin/rpmsg-eth) is hand-staged per rpmsg-dualboot.md and is
# not in the image, so enabling it would put a unit in the boot path that
# cannot run on a freshly flashed board. It is not left unreachable by the
# omission: both bridges (awf-oak-bridge and the demo stack's
# x5h-demo-bridge) carry Requires=rpmsg-eth.service, so the link is pulled
# up whenever a stack that needs it starts, and the unit's own
# ConditionPathExists= makes an unstaged binary a skipped unit with one
# journal line rather than a failure or a restart loop.
#
# awf-oak-x5h-extract-map.service was enabled here until the nine-unit set
# was retired. Both the unit and the kashiwanoha map it extracted are gone
# (the MRM scenario ships its own matched map, staged onto the board by
# scripts/stage-scenario-map.sh), so the line was naming a unit that no
# longer exists and had to go with it.
#
# cr52-remoteproc.service is enabled now that its script ships in the
# image; on a board without a staged ELF it logs
# CR52_RPROC_SKIP reason=no_firmware and exits 0, and under yocto its
# condition skips it. rpmsg-eth.service is still NOT enabled (standing
# ruling: its binary is hand-staged).
enable sshd.service
enable x5h-role-banner.service
enable var-lib-containers.mount
enable var-opt-npu.mount
enable x5h-npu.service
enable cr52-remoteproc.service
